 reaction as  succinate and are omitting the coenzyme  a for clarity in the fifth step  succinylcholine xym a is converted into  succinate by succinylcholine that is  releasing coenzyme a this reaction also  produces one molecule of GTP another  high-energy molecule which is emitted  from this diagram for clarity in the  sixth step succinate is oxidized to  fumarate by succinate dehydrogenase  unlike all the other enzymes in the  citric acid cycle succinate  dehydrogenase is embedded in the inner  mitochondrial membrane and is also a  component of the electron transport  chain in which it is also called complex  2 as complex 2 oxidizes succinate it  receives two electrons that it will  ultimately pass on to coenzyme q which  in turn will deliver its electrons to  complex 3 another interesting aspect of  complex 2 is that it uses fa d rather  than nad plus to accept electrons in the  seventh step fumarate is converted to  malate by the enzyme fumarate and  finally in the eighth step the enzyme  malate dehydrogenase oxidizes malate to  reform oxaloacetate and reduces a  molecule of NAD+ to NADH in the process  this regenerated oxaloacetate can then  combine with another acetylcholine in  the next cycle  you  [Music]

